KW  - Lithium-ion battery
KW  - Remaining useful life prediction
KW  - Deep state observer
KW  - Interpretable model
AB  - Accurate prediction of the remaining useful life (RUL) of lithium-ion batteries is critical yet challenging due to complex nonlinear degradation, while existing data-driven methods often lack interpretability and fail to capture underlying physical dynamics. To address this, we propose a Deep Stacked State Observer Network (DSONN) that innovatively integrates an extended state observer with deep neural networks for physics-informed RUL prediction. Its novelty lies in three aspects: (1) embedding discretized ESO neurons with state-space dynamics into the network architecture for physically interpretable joint learning; (2) designing a serial deep stacking structure that hierarchically abstracts degradation features from short-term fluctuations to long-term trends via progressive state estimation; and (3) introducing a mechanism-inspired nonlinear correction term using the fal function to explicitly capture complex phenomena such as capacity plunge. Using charging-phase and relaxation-phase voltage from two public datasets, DSONN achieves 39.6% and 4.4% RMSE reduction over the EKIDM baseline on Datasets 1 and 2 respectively, with ablation studies confirming the contributions of each innovation. This work presents a modeling paradigm that balances accuracy with interpretability for battery RUL prediction.
