AB  - In power systems of 35 kV and above, harmonic measurements are not easy to implement due to the uneven frequency responses of widely used capacitor-coupled voltage transformers (CCVTs). In this paper, a compensation method derived from a model representing the voltage transfer characteristics of CCVTs is proposed to monitor harmonics in power systems with existing CCVTs. Low-voltage harmonic and frequency-sweep tests are designed to determine the employed parameters in the compensation method. Several designed harmonic tests are conducted on a 35 kV CCVT to verify the proposed compensation and parameter determination methods. The results of the experiments show that the proposed methods have the potential of saving large investments in harmonic measurement.
